            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic pain in women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>566-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical and psychological characteristics of 18 women with pelvic pain but no demonstrable pathology have been compared with those of 17 women with a similar complaint but some form of pelvic pathology and a control group of 9 women with no gynecologic problems. The results suggest that pelvic pain can have a psychosomatic origin which is amenable to short-term psychotherapeutic measures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
